        "original_id": "cbcd1abd-e1be-565b-942f-c250ee61f976",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Alexandra Park, Oldham; North West England\n- Events: Lancashire Cotton Famine; Cotton Panic\n- Topics: textile industry; local textile workers; employment\n\nFacts:\n- The Lancashire Cotton Famine, also known as the Cotton Famine or the Cotton Panic, took place from 1861 to 1865.\n- The Lancashire Cotton Famine was a depression in the textile industry of North West England.\n- The Lancashire Cotton Famine was caused by overproduction during a period of contracting world markets.\n- Alexandra Park in Oldham was created in response to the Lancashire Cotton Famine of 1861 to 1865.\n- Alexandra Park in Oldham was created as an attempt to keep local textile workers employed.",
